cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "From Cloud to Assembly Line: Modelling Cyberattack Paths in Automotive Manufacturing as Critical Infrastructure"
message: "If you use this model, corpus or artefact, please cite it."
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-16
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rikosoo/InfraCriticalCar"
abstract: >-
  A cross-plane attack-path model (CAPM) of an automotive assembly plant
  spanning corporate IT, the identity plane, cloud and SaaS, the industrial DMZ,
  MES/SCADA/PLC layers and the supplier interface, calibrated against a corpus
  of 20 publicly reported incidents in automotive manufacturing (2017-2025),
  with MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise and ICS technique labelling and controls mapped
  to IEC 62443-3-3 and NIST CSF 2.0.
keywords:
  - critical infrastructure
  - automotive manufacturing
  - attack graphs
  - operational technology
  - MITRE ATT&CK
  - IEC 62443
  - risk quantification
